## Output Format

Return only one valid JSON object. Do not use markdown fences, XML tags, or text outside the JSON object.

{% if case_grounding|default(true) %}
Assess every memory independently in display order. Output exactly {{ (miss_memories|length) + (normal_memories|length) }} case_assessments: miss ranks 1 through {{ miss_memories|length }}, then success ranks 1 through {{ normal_memories|length }}.
For each memory, choose one impact: support means its complete observed action is useful to imitate; conflict means an observable mismatch reduces its influence; irrelevant means it adds no useful evidence. Give one or two free-form lowercase factors. Each factor must be a 1-4 word noun phrase about only this memory, such as "same smash" or "instruction aligned"; use adjectives, never verb clauses.{% if semantic_enabled|default(true) %} Twin or instruction context may be a factor only when explicitly stated and observably supported.{% else %} Instruction context may be a factor only when observably supported.{% endif %} No sentences, explanations, conjunctions, numbers, coordinates, labels, ranks inside factors, or references to other memories. Use every required source/rank exactly once. Then output the action directly.
